Keep a caller-selected RAW white in the decoder. Temperature/tint controls
already know the scene white; deriving its illuminant again from camera
multipliers can select a different root of a dual-illuminant DNG profile.
Existing multiplier-only and as-shot entry points retain their behaviour.

